<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's net reserves rise to $1.97 bln on Apr 18.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's net reserves rise to $1.97 bln on Apr 18.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Tuesday its net international reserves stood at $1.97 billion on April 18, up $4 million from the week before.</p>
<p>In March 1997, international reserves grew $139 million.</p>
<p>Reserves stood at $1.832 billion at the end of 1996, up $274 million from the end of 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
